# Build artifacts
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dSYM/

# Test binaries
#
# The named rules below are an allowlist, and an allowlist of built artifacts
# only holds until someone adds a test. It did not hold: test_geojson, test_eov,
# test_metatile and four copies of test_transport_direct were committed as
# macOS arm64 executables, which broke the Windows job -- `./test_geojson`
# found the Mach-O file instead of test_geojson.exe and exited 126.
#
# So ignore built test binaries by shape instead. These patterns are anchored
# with a leading slash and contain no further slash, so each matches only a
# DIRECT child of that module directory -- where the Makefiles put their
# executables. Test *sources* live in <module>/tests/ and are unaffected.
/arbor/test_*
/carta/test_*
/clayshards/test_*
/fuelwise/test_*
/locus/test_*
/nexus/test_*
/ralph/test_*
/shared/test_*
/surge/test_*
/velo/test_*

test_ralph
test_fuelwise
test_shared
test_pal

# Windows builds the same binaries with an .exe suffix, so every rule
# above would otherwise miss them. Nothing tracked ends in .exe.
*.exe
test_velo
test_carta
test_font
test_lap
test_lap_dbg
test_lap_debug
test_locus

